confirm_other.description:
New address: {url}

Another BamBuddy server: the history of the server's own figures (print statistics, storage …) is deleted. The printers under “Kept” keep theirs.

**Smart plugs** of the printers under “Kept” come from the new server, each as a new device: an area or name you gave a plug device starts afresh. A plug that uses the same Tasmota, Home Assistant entity or MQTT topic as before keeps its entity IDs and history; the others get new ones. Plugs the new server does not have for them are removed.

**Kept:**
{kept}

**Removed** (with their AMS units and smart plugs):
{removed}

**Added:**
{added}

Choose “Switch” to apply this; close the dialog to leave everything as it is.

confirm.description:
BamBuddy now reports AMS serial numbers of {name} that it did not report before. From now on each of these units is known by its serial number — its device, entities and history stay — and its entity IDs carry it instead of the printer's serial number:

- {renamed}

Home Assistant does not change automations, scripts and dashboards for you; the BamBuddy card finds the units by itself. Update those that use the old IDs. Entity IDs you had changed yourself stay as they were. Once everything uses the new IDs, choose “Done” to close this notice.
